From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 23:11:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: review Chronik producer schemas and preserve bridge
 regression control

Record explicit per-site review for all28 Chronik C++ legacy consumers. The14
native WebSocket LogDebug calls use a local message callback, not BCLog's
category macro. Three generic host/Rust adapters already receive text; typed
schemas belong in upstream caller/host-neutral APIs. Ten subscriber/lifecycle
consumers remain deferred for coordinated canonical Chronik ownership.

Preserve the bridge's BRIDGE_BARRIER legacy Error call as a regression control:
replacing the interface under test with an event would change the quota/drain
control path. This is one explicit intentional test marker, not an application
schema exemption. No production files or logging behavior changed.

Review reproduction:
python3 /Users/shammah/repos/lotus-v2-repair-work/logging-cleanup/review_chronik_inventory.py

Validation: all-source inventory fixture PASS, exact IDs inspected against
af414ca13af4eefec9f07ddc4037818bae2a7ca5; diff check clean. No suites or builds
needed for disposition metadata. A separate inventory-owner fixup classifies
chronik/test/ as tests, with a reproduced-before/passes-after fixture.

